            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "crazycatlady"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My life has been much happier since I discovered this recipe 3 years ago. I use frozen bananas (stored in a gallon bag in the freezer so I can make this delicious margarita whenever the mood strikes), and fill my one-cup measuring cup full of ice. That helps it stay frozen.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-05T19:39:10.010Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jodell Roberts"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Mix was a little more tart than the one I had at the Mexican restuarant. I will cut back on the lemon and lime juice next time. Used store bought ice, filled to 6 cup line, and consistency was perfect. Dipped rim in lime juice then sugar. Was a nice touch! Pretty good!",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-30T17:22:02.590Z"
          },
          {
